# A directory, a file, or a symlink to one. The trailing slash meant only a real
# directory, so in a linked worktree - where the way to point the data-driven
# tests at the collection is `ln -s /path/to/main/test-roms test-roms` - the
# symlink showed up as untracked and one `git add -A` away from being committed
# with an absolute path in it (#251).
/test-roms
*.srm
*.state
.direnv/
result
result-*
# Never commit ROMs.
*.md.rom
*.gen
*.smd
*.bin
